      "message": "I think we can broaden this case. We can run into situations where `SkColorSpaceXformSteps` doesn\u0027t think we need to linearize the input or encode the output (e.g. the src or dst SkColorSpace was srgb_linear_singleton()).  In those cases we may not get the premul specialization if we still have one-side requiring a transfer function, or adjusting the gamut.\n\nIn those cases, it\u0027s probably better to set values in the sRGB-ish coefficients to have it be an identity function vs. going to the universal snippet.",
