      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-22T16:38:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "noPremul update:\n\n    // identity:        {0,  1}\n    // do unpremul:     {-1, 1}\n    // do premul:       {0,  0}\n    // alpha-swizzle 1: {1,  1}\n    // alpha-swizzle r: {1,  0}\n\nWhen we calculate the premul value, matching the sk_color_space_transform_premul specialization, we could do:\n\n    color.rgb \u003d half3(colorF.rgb) * max(color.a, noPremul);\n\nIn the alpha-swizzle cases, RGB should be 0 so it doesn\u0027t matter if we multiply with color.a or with 1.\n\nWe can also update the `alphaSwizzleMask` to be:\n\n    half alphaSwizzle1 \u003d dstDEF_args.w;\n    half alphaSwizzleR \u003d srcDEF_args.w - dstDEF_args.w;\n    half3(1.0 - srcDEF_args.w, alphaSwizzleR, alphaSwizzle1)\n    \nand if we put it in the `else` block after the unpremul case, we can drop the clamp around it. The alpha swizzle dot product can also be inside this else branch because we won\u0027t be using an alpha swizzle if we premul.\n\nThe color transforms and premul operations can\u0027t be in the else, though none of the args values would mess up the values.",
